From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +01:00
Subject: [PATCH] fix: round multi-host worker group scale up to whole replica steps to prevent fractional grants

Partial scale-up grants fractional worker slices to multi-host Ray worker groups, creating incomplete node sets that cannot initialize distributed communication frameworks and leaving pods permanently unscheduled.

Multi-host Ray worker groups operate in gang-scheduled increments of numOfHosts pods that must be scheduled together to establish collective communication runtimes. Standard elastic partial scale-up divides available quota linearly, inadvertently allocating partial slices that do not align with multi-host gang boundaries.

Enforce whole-replica step increments during partial scale-up for workloads implementing JobWithPodSetCountSteps, rounding admitted worker counts down to integer multiples of numOfHosts. Workload slice controllers reject fractional allocations and wait until sufficient queue quota exists to admit complete multi-host worker groups.
---
